INT. BELLTOWER OBSERVATORY - NIGHT

A cramped brass-and-oak room at the top of a church tower. Star charts curl on the walls. A telescope points through a roof hatch.

PROFESSOR AMBROSE QUILL (70s, cardigan, wire spectacles) sits at a desk, writing in a leather journal. He pauses. Taps his pen. Lifts his head as though listening.

He rises, crosses to a brass speaking tube on the wall, and uncaps it.

AMBROSE
(into tube)
Mrs. Pennywhistle?

SEXTON (V.O.)
(distant, tinny)
Yes, Professor?

AMBROSE
Did you take the key to the lower cabinet?

SEXTON (V.O.)
No, sir. It was on its hook at supper.

He frowns. Looks to the cabinet. The door is ajar.

AMBROSE
It is not there now.

SEXTON (V.O.)
Shall I come up?

He considers. Glances at the journal on the desk, then at the dark hatch above.

AMBROSE
No. Thank you. I believe I know where it is.

He caps the tube. Returns to his desk. Opens a drawer. The key lies inside, dusted with chalk.

He smiles faintly. Closes the drawer.
